WEBVTT

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:05.769
On the Mcbe2Friends project page, choose
Download for Windows to get the

00:00:05.769 --> 00:00:10.635
standalone EXE. Mac and Linux downloads
are in the download chest.

00:00:10.835 --> 00:00:15.092
Double-click Mcbe2Friends.exe. The
launcher opens in its own window.

00:00:15.092 --> 00:00:18.749
On Mac or Linux, open the app from the
extracted download.

00:00:19.487 --> 00:00:22.964
Already have a running server? Enter its
Bedrock address and port.

00:00:23.164 --> 00:00:26.748
The usual port is 19132. Choose
Continue.

00:00:27.487 --> 00:00:31.391
Use a dedicated Microsoft account with
an Xbox gamertag.

00:00:31.591 --> 00:00:34.663
Choose whether to accept friend requests
automatically,

00:00:34.663 --> 00:00:36.305
then select Connect & start.

00:00:37.028 --> 00:00:40.552
The launcher sets up Java if needed.
When a code appears,

00:00:40.552 --> 00:00:42.490
choose Open Microsoft sign-in.

00:00:42.690 --> 00:00:46.167
Enter your own code on Microsoft’s page
and finish signing in.

00:00:46.903 --> 00:00:51.001
Wait for Broadcast live, then give
friends the broadcaster’s Xbox

00:00:51.001 --> 00:00:51.725
gamertag.

00:00:51.925 --> 00:00:55.337
Once their requests are accepted, they
open Minecraft Bedrock,

00:00:55.337 --> 00:00:58.172
choose Play, then Friends, and select
your session.

00:00:58.903 --> 00:01:02.875
Keep the host PC awake. Closing the
launcher window leaves your Friends

00:01:02.875 --> 00:01:04.002
broadcast running.

00:01:04.202 --> 00:01:06.777
Use Stop broadcast to end it. Next time,

00:01:06.777 --> 00:01:09.173
Start broadcast reuses your settings.

00:01:09.903 --> 00:01:13.061
To host a new world on your own PC, open
Premium.

00:01:13.261 --> 00:01:17.909
Java runs on Windows, macOS, and Linux.
For native Bedrock,

00:01:17.909 --> 00:01:21.133
use a supported Windows or Linux x64 PC.

00:01:21.862 --> 00:01:24.782
Copy your PC code, choose Get Premium on
Discord,

00:01:24.782 --> 00:01:26.747
and send the code to the seller.

00:01:26.947 --> 00:01:31.372
After the one-time $15 purchase, paste
the key you receive and choose

00:01:31.372 --> 00:01:32.110
Activate.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:37.589
In Premium, open Java Edition. Name your
server and pick your friends’

00:01:37.589 --> 00:01:40.137
Minecraft version, from 1.19 onward.

00:01:40.337 --> 00:01:44.796
Pick Vanilla for a classic world, Fabric
for mods, or Paper for plugins.

00:01:45.528 --> 00:01:49.354
For cross-play, select Paper + Geyser on
a compatible release.

00:01:49.354 --> 00:01:53.592
Review the Minecraft terms, check the
box, and choose Create & start.

00:01:53.792 --> 00:01:56.224
When it says Running, open How to join.

00:01:56.224 --> 00:01:58.946
Java players use Multiplayer and Add
Server.

00:01:58.946 --> 00:02:01.899
Bedrock friends use the Geyser address
and port.

00:02:02.099 --> 00:02:05.180
The local address works at home. For
internet play,

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:09.288
forward the displayed ports to this PC
and share your public address.

00:02:10.028 --> 00:02:13.274
Stop Paper before importing a plugin.
Enable the plugin,

00:02:13.274 --> 00:02:15.255
then start the server to load it.

00:02:15.455 --> 00:02:19.728
In Settings & cross-play, you can turn
Geyser on or off while keeping the

00:02:19.728 --> 00:02:22.708
same world. Save the change before
starting again.

00:02:22.908 --> 00:02:25.679
Under Worlds & backups, back up a
stopped world.

00:02:25.679 --> 00:02:29.266
Restore into a new folder and select it
in Settings to play it.

00:02:29.987 --> 00:02:34.616
For a modded server, pick Fabric and
choose Create only. This world,

00:02:34.616 --> 00:02:36.963
Moss Hollow, uses Minecraft 1.19.

00:02:37.163 --> 00:02:41.325
Open Fabric mods and search Modrinth.
Choose a version of Ledger that

00:02:41.325 --> 00:02:44.331
matches your server, then select Install
version.

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:49.621
Ledger is installed, along with Fabric
API and Fabric Language Kotlin.

00:02:49.621 --> 00:02:51.491
All three are enabled here.

00:02:51.691 --> 00:02:55.536
Review and accept the Minecraft terms.
Choose Start server and wait for

00:02:55.536 --> 00:02:56.107
Running.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:03:00.376
With Moss Hollow running, choose Close
launcher or use the close button

00:03:00.376 --> 00:03:01.385
on the app window.

00:03:01.585 --> 00:03:03.714
The server keeps running on this PC.

00:03:03.714 --> 00:03:07.481
Your Bedrock server or Friends broadcast
can also stay on with the

00:03:07.481 --> 00:03:08.519
launcher closed.

00:03:09.237 --> 00:03:13.589
Here is the server’s reply to Minecraft
with the launcher closed.

00:03:13.589 --> 00:03:17.237
Reopen Mcbe2Friends to manage that same
running world.

00:03:17.437 --> 00:03:19.956
If the host PC restarts, sign back in.

00:03:19.956 --> 00:03:23.581
Servers and broadcasts you left on
resume automatically.

00:03:24.320 --> 00:03:27.025
To take your world offline, choose Stop
server.

00:03:27.025 --> 00:03:30.272
Use Stop broadcast separately to end the
Friends listing.

00:03:30.472 --> 00:03:34.346
Each Stop also turns off automatic
restart for that service until you

00:03:34.346 --> 00:03:35.315
start it again.

00:03:36.028 --> 00:03:39.780
For a native Bedrock world, select
Bedrock Edition in Premium.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:43.474
Review the Minecraft terms and choose
Install & start server.

00:03:43.674 --> 00:03:46.231
Wait for Server running before inviting
friends.

00:03:46.945 --> 00:03:51.279
Under Players & Friends tab, enter a
friend’s Xbox gamertag and choose

00:03:51.279 --> 00:03:53.238
Allow. Repeat for each player.

00:03:53.438 --> 00:03:57.448
Players on your network can also join
using the local address and server

00:03:57.448 --> 00:03:57.876
port.

00:03:58.612 --> 00:04:03.784
For internet play, forward the server
port for both TCP and UDP to the

00:04:03.784 --> 00:04:04.564
host PC.

00:04:04.764 --> 00:04:07.029
Enter an address your friends can reach,

00:04:07.029 --> 00:04:09.926
then choose Friends setup and follow the
Xbox steps.

00:04:10.653 --> 00:04:13.341
While the server is running, open Server
console.

00:04:13.541 --> 00:04:15.888
Send the list command to see who is
online.

00:04:16.612 --> 00:04:19.492
Choose Stop server to save the world
before editing.

00:04:19.692 --> 00:04:22.800
Open Server settings & worlds. Choose a
world,

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:26.860
adjust the player slots or use PC
recommendations, then save.

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:31.460
Under Add-ons, choose your .mcaddon or
.mcpack file and click Import

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:32.007
add-on.

00:04:32.207 --> 00:04:36.389
Enable each required resource and
behavior pack for the selected world.

00:04:37.112 --> 00:04:40.783
Under World imports & backups, choose
Back up selected world.

00:04:40.783 --> 00:04:43.192
Open backups to find the .mcworld file.

00:04:43.392 --> 00:04:47.961
If the old world folder still exists,
use Open server folder. In worlds,

00:04:47.961 --> 00:04:50.581
rename the old folder to keep your copy.

00:04:50.781 --> 00:04:54.541
Choose the .mcworld, enter the original
world name for the new folder,

00:04:54.541 --> 00:04:55.880
and click Import world.

00:04:56.612 --> 00:05:00.772
Select the restored world in settings,
save, and start the server again.

00:05:00.972 --> 00:05:03.520
With the host PC awake and the broadcast
live,

00:05:03.520 --> 00:05:05.601
your friends can get back to playing.
